rewrite_suggestion:
Add supporting composite indexes (inspired by Cases 1 and 2). Because lineitem is the largest table, indexes that let the optimizer start from the most selective dimension filters help most:

- lineitem(l_orderkey, l_suppkey, l_extendedprice, l_discount) — covering index for the join and revenue computation;
- orders(o_orderdate, o_orderkey, o_custkey) — range scan on orderdate returning join keys only (covering);
- supplier(s_suppkey, s_nationkey);
- nation(n_nationkey, n_regionkey, n_name) and region(r_regionkey, r_name) — small dimension covering indexes.

The orders index ordered by o_orderdate first lets the date-range predicate prune rows immediately rather than scanning all orders.

